  "Question": "Given \\(x=51\\) and \\(y=49\\), find the value of \\(3x^2-3y^2\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "600",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(3x^2-3y^2=3(x+y)(x-y)=3\\times100\\times2=600\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Substitute and calculate directly\n\nBecause both variable values are given, we can evaluate the two terms directly. Since \\(51^2=2601\\) and \\(49^2=2401\\),\n\\[\n3x^2-3y^2=3\\cdot2601-3\\cdot2401\n=7803-7203=600.\n\\]",
